@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### Application information
GET {{baseUrl}}/

### List clothes and inspect custom response headers
GET {{baseUrl}}/clothes

### Case-insensitive search
GET {{baseUrl}}/clothes?search=SWEAT

### Limit filtered results
GET {{baseUrl}}/clothes?search=sweat&limit=1

### Find seeded item
GET {{baseUrl}}/clothes/1

### Missing item returns 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/clothes/99999

### Create an item before running the following requests
# @name createClothing
POST {{baseUrl}}/clothes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Cotton T-Shirt",
  "price": 850,
  "size": "M",
  "material": "Cotton",
  "color": "Lavender"
}

### Read created item
GET {{baseUrl}}/clothes/{{createClothing.response.body.$.id}}

### Partially update the created item
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/clothes/{{createClothing.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "price": 790,
  "color": "Black"
}

### Delete created item and verify 204 with an empty body
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/clothes/{{createClothing.response.body.$.id}}

### Deleted item returns 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/clothes/{{createClothing.response.body.$.id}}

### Invalid price returns 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/clothes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Cotton T-Shirt",
  "price": -1,
  "size": "M",
  "material": "Cotton",
  "color": "Lavender"
}

### Invalid limit returns 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/clothes?limit=0

### Replacing the primary key is rejected
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/clothes/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "replacement"
}
